  "result": "Perfect! All 94 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n**New file `src/render.js`:**\n- **`renderInvoiceText(invoice)`** \u2014 Renders an invoice as plain text\n\nThe output format is:\n```\nINV-2025-0001\nCustomer Name\n5 \u00d7 Development (hour) @ \u20ac95.00 = \u20ac475.00\n3 \u00d7 Design work (hour) @ \u20ac85.00 = \u20ac255.00\nTotal: \u20ac730.00\n```\n\nFeatures:\n- First line shows invoice number (or `DRAFT` if not yet issued)\n- Second line shows customer name (fetched from customers module)\n- One line per invoice line with: `qty \u00d7 name @ unitPrice = lineTotal`\n- All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()` from src/money.js\n- Last line shows the total\n- Gracefully handles unknown customers with \"Unknown Customer\" fallback\n- Correctly calculates totals from all line items\n\n**Added 15 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Draft vs. issued invoice number display\n- Customer name inclusion\n- Line item formatting with all required fields\n- Price formatting with thousands separators and two decimals\n- Total calculation for single and multiple lines\n- Different customers and VAT rates\n- Large quantities and single-quantity items\n- Unknown customer fallback\n- Output structure and newline handling\n- Integration with `createInvoice()` and `issueInvoice()`\n\nAll customer-facing amounts go through `formatEuros()` for consistent formatting. \u2713",
